igned area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in (0,4].$ The corresponding region is a rectangle below the $x$-axis, so the signed area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =(4)(1) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{A}_{2}=-4.\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-4}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\, & =\\,{A}_{1}+{A}_{2} \\\\  & =\\,8+(-4) \\\\  & =\\,4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068433/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f5ce626556a3e0e0a7ec4452a843198291f8862c0987f5017f309f08187bfa7"} {"question" "q-338316" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068433/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2049c2661b2ac1a9129510ff2d23585815c53ff67aad11198fd6bc9dd5eaee53"} {"question" "q-338316" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068433/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f5ce626556a3e0e0a7ec4452a843198291f8862c0987f5017f309f08187bfa7"} {"question" "q-338316" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068433/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f5ce626556a3e0e0a7ec4452a843198291f8862c0987f5017f309f08187bfa7"}] "usage" {"q-117680" [] "q-49215" []} "basis" 2335 "retractions" [[17592186306198 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040192/assets/11cf2a28b6ce6281de0299a4a585bc3c98bf891f6d958401f22aab2fc6ce5ef2.png)\n\nGiven the graph of $y=f(x)$ above, find th